@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@ and this project follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).
 - **Typing progress bar.** Optional bar above the entry box showing how much of the phrase is correct so far, updated as you type (*Settings > Look*, `show_typing_progress`, off by default).
 - **Keep what I typed correctly after a typo.** *Settings > Rules*: instead of clearing the entry box after a mistake, keep the correctly typed beginning and carry on from there (`keep_correct_on_error`, off by default). Independent from "Reset the counter to 0 on a typo".
 - **Switch style from the tray.** Right-click the tray icon > **Style** lists the theme packs (yours included) with a tick on the current one. Switching applies the pack exactly like *Apply* in Settings (protections are never changed) and asks for the emergency password first when one is set. New `styleswitch.py` and the `--switch-style` argument.
-- **Background drop zone.** *Settings > Look > Background* has a box where you can drag PNG, JPG, WEBP, BMP or GIF files from Explorer to add them to the background list (clicking the box opens the file picker). Other files are ignored with a message. Windows only, no extra package. New `dropfiles.py`.
+- **Background gallery.** *Settings > Look > Background* now shows your background images and GIFs as small pictures (GIFs carry a GIF badge, online URLs and missing files get a labelled placeholder) in a compact grid that scrolls when there are many. Each picture has a **×** button to remove it. Pictures load one by one so a long list never freezes the window. The old text list and its "Remove selected" button are gone.
+- **Background drop zone.** *Settings > Look > Background* has a box where you can drag PNG, JPG, WEBP, BMP or GIF files from Explorer to add them to the background list (clicking the box opens the file picker). Other files are ignored with a message. Windows only, no extra package. New `dropfiles.py`, `gallery.py`.
 - **Open the settings folder / the log file.** Two buttons in *Settings > Home*. New `openpaths.py`.
 - **Phrase file editor.** *Settings > Phrases > Create or edit a phrase file...* opens a window to build a phrase file without touching a text editor: a table of phrases (with category and difficulty), a form to add, update and delete, a box to paste many phrases at once (`phrase | category | difficulty`, tabs from a spreadsheet work too), file import, duplicate removal, sort by difficulty and warnings for very long phrases. It starts from your current file or the built-in list and saves a CSV, JSON or TXT file (in `%APPDATA%\PhraseLock\phrases` by default) that PhraseLock can use right away. New `phraseeditor.py`.
 - **Crash-loop guard.** If the background monitor fails to start 5 times in 10 minutes, or the Auto-protection watchdog has to restart it 5 times in 10 minutes, PhraseLock turns itself off instead of looping: `enabled` and `auto_protection` are set to false, the watchdog stops, the reason goes to `phraselock.log` and `crash_guard.json`, and *Settings > Home* shows a red notice with a **Turn protection back on** button. A monitor that stays up for 3 minutes starts counting from zero again, so occasional restarts never trip it. New `crashguard.py`.
